{"agent":"bugfix8","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_substitutions` / `_scan` bodies are never read by `_split` or any other caller in this change, so a forbidden command that only runs inside `$(...)` or backticks is still allowed. Given `echo $(git push origin main)` (and the same with a newline inside the substitution), bash runs `git push`, but `_split` only shlexes the outer logical line, whose command word is `echo`, and `check` does not refuse it. The same miss covers `` echo `git push origin main` ``.","digest":"95af7386d062218e","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_substitutions","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_substitutions"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The `case`/`esac` walk treats a bare `esac` as the keyword and never skips `#` comments (or quotes), so a `)` in that comment is then taken as the `$()` closer. Given:\n```\necho \"$(case x in\nx) echo start # esac )\ngit push origin main;;\nesac)\"\n```\nbash comments out `# esac )` and runs `git push origin main` in the case arm. `_find_body` drops depth on the comment's `esac`, returns at the comment's `)`, and records a body that stops before `git push`. The remainder stays inside the outer double quotes, so it is neither a substitution body nor a top-level command, and the guard does not refuse it.","digest":"eda8d3a5bfc4f1ce","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_find_body","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_find_body"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12639,"diff_sha":"f0a4215c7f19aec4283d595a3adc917c08841f1554982ad4f248a3fafa780162","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":235.0,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"3c88076c7739910e","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-forbidden-guard-multiline-quote-bypass.critic.grok-4.7.20261105T214805Z-d94cd7c6.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"7a36fa7f2cbe5a2d7cd941988b4f442eab5a3887","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/forbidden.py":"100644 776d3aab2b7cb95727c5c65d51f094e6727999ce","tests/test_forbidden_commands.py":"100644 a1ac29e1164e2be8704466baa6ddf3dda8a800b4"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["xai"],"round":6,"rounds":6,"status":"REVIEWED","superseded":["a4deba572ee703e9"],"titles":["ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_substitutions","ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_find_body"],"tree_sha":"7a36fa7f2cbe+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e34f6bda7428bbf16d6a0776b","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":143487,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-forbidden-guard-multiline-quote-bypass","ts":"2026-11-05T21:52:00.879671Z"}
