{"agent":"bugfix8","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"budget_forced":"verify d5f683d83 fixes critic #2 (case-body comment skip); budget spent","chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The `case`/`esac` walk added in `_find_body` still matches `esac` without skipping quotes, so a word-boundary `esac` and a following `)` inside a quote close the substitution early and drop the real command. Given `echo \"$(case x in x) echo ' esac )' git push origin main;; esac)\"`, bash runs `git push origin main` in the case arm (`' esac )'` is only an argument to `echo`). The walk treats the quoted `esac` as the keyword (`' '` is a word boundary in `_bare_word`), depth hits 0, then the quoted `)` is taken as the `$(` closer. The recorded body stops before `git push`, and the outer command word is `echo`, so `check` does not refuse it.","digest":"b64996339f140f10","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:185","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:185"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":13016,"diff_sha":"15f4aaebbee1fb2901ae9dd5797efc5bbc9423c5f6640e5f1e71c1854dfda242","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":94.5,"family":"xai","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"6767d4bd0bd60ac3","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-forbidden-guard-multiline-quote-bypass.critic.grok-4.7.20261105T215716Z-9f13ed5a.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"d5f683d838efad76049e4f210f43600c0916e300","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/forbidden.py":"100644 2ebcfaf905e4a7a04e10ccf73cbb48fc1214f34e","tests/test_forbidden_commands.py":"100644 bbf235fe0d9be38c63c15bd7d9d350b2febf4e85"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["xai"],"round":7,"rounds":7,"status":"REVIEWED","superseded":["a4deba572ee703e9"],"titles":["d